Use Qt's existing runtime OS-version check for SecureTransport's macOS 15 import.

Darwin cross-builds do not supply Clang's __isPlatformVersionAtLeast helper.
QOperatingSystemVersion preserves the macOS 15 memory-only key import and the
older temporary-keychain fallback without that compiler runtime dependency.
Peer certificate, hostname and TLS protocol verification are unchanged.

--- a/qtbase/src/plugins/tls/securetransport/qtls_st.cpp
+++ b/qtbase/src/plugins/tls/securetransport/qtls_st.cpp
@@ -823,7 +823,7 @@ bool TlsCryptographSecureTransport::setSessionCertificate(QString &errorDescription
         // instead. This key is "memory" but looks like Security framework
         // does not compare strings, but pointers instead, so we need an actual
         // key/constant.
-        if (__builtin_available(macOS 15, *)) {
+        if (QOperatingSystemVersion::current() >= QOperatingSystemVersion::MacOSSequoia) {
             nKeys = 2;
             keys[1] = kSecImportToMemoryOnly;
             values[1] = kCFBooleanTrue;
